<title>UK: TABLE-BA headline profits rise in Q1.</title>
<headline>TABLE-BA headline profits rise in Q1.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		16.3		   vs 11.9</p>
<p> Pretax		     220		    vs 150</p>
<p> Turnover		   2.22 bln	     vs 2.10</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts had forecast underlying pre-tax profits in a range between 115 and 155 million stg.</p>
<p>Headline profits were boosted by an exceptional gain of 130 million stg from the sale of BA's former partner US Air.</p>
<p>BA also announced that it carried 8.95 million passengers in the first quarter compared with 8.50 million in the comparitive period a year ago.</p>
<p>Overall load factor rose to 69.8 percent from 69.4.</p>
<p>Passenger revenue per RPK was 6.44p versus 6.60, while cargo revenue per CTK was 14.34p versus 15.15p.</p>
<p>Full company name - British Airways Plc.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
